WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.540
Every bad guy in the world could be gunning
for the Brunners at the end of FUBAR Season 1.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.010
From twisted love triangles to shattered secret
lives, let's break down how they got there

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.432
and where they go next.

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:14.700
Arnold Schwarzenegger is back in his element
in Netflix's action comedy, "FUBAR."

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.250
He stars as CIA agent Luke Brunner who is
nearing retirement.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.689
That's when he discovers his daughter, Emma,
has also been keeping the same secret from

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:23.939
the family and working as an operative.

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:27.460
After discovering Emma's secret, Luke works
together with her and a team consisting of

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.420
Aldon, Roo, Barry, and Tina.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.410
Their main mission is to take down an international
terrorist and arms dealer, Boro.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.860
The group gets close a few times, but the
season sees them often having to shake up

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.860
their approach.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.470
Turns out, their man is a bit of a slippery
customer who has his own network of bad guys

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.810
doing his bidding.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.540
The other story of "FUBAR" is how Luke and
Emma's personal lives continue to suffer due

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.217
to their top-secret work.

00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:51.680
Luke tries to encourage his daughter to learn
from his mistakes and not repeat them, but

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.570
this only accelerates her issues.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.201
"Take your daughter to work day is going well."

00:00:56.201 --> 00:00:59.950
She and her fiancé, Carter, break up after
she starts snogging her colleague, Aldon,

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.100
whom she has conflicted feelings for.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.930
Similarly, Luke has his relationship woes
as he rekindles the romance with his ex-wife,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.849
Tally, whom he has never gotten over.

00:01:07.849 --> 00:01:11.980
There's a problem there, though: Tally is
in a relationship with Donnie, but she promises

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.600
she will break it off for Luke.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.930
After Luke breaks her heart for the second
time -- in what he deems an effort to spare

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.253
her from further pain -- Tally takes the plunge
and decides she wants to commit and marry Donnie.

00:01:21.253 --> 00:01:25.530
"FUBAR" Season 1 ends on an action-packed
note that ties up a few loose threads, but

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.030
also introduces a bunch of new ones into the
mix.

00:01:28.356 --> 00:01:32.380
Luke makes a big call in the season finale
after Emma and Boro work together to try and

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.340
avoid the impending explosion in Sardovia
. While Luke has the ability to help Boro

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.380
out of danger, he decides against it, fearing
that he will come after his family later on.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.188
"You gave me your word.

00:01:41.188 --> 00:01:42.188
Let me out."

00:01:42.351 --> 00:01:43.242
"I'm sorry.

00:01:43.242 --> 00:01:44.872
I can't let you come after her."

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.899
Despite his closeness to the criminal as a
child and his previous reluctance, Luke leaves

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:52.200
the villain to perish in the nuclear explosion
and escapes with his daughter.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.480
Back home, Luke announces his official retirement
from the CIA and gets blindsided by the news

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.200
that Tally is marrying Donnie.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.079
Initially, he accepts the decision and wishes
both Tally and Donnie well, despite having

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:04.049
no plans to attend the wedding.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:07.779
Emma eggs her father on, though, telling him
to fight for her mother and what he wants.

00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:09.416
"I'm trying to be the bigger man."

00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:11.075
"You're being the dumber man."

00:02:11.075 --> 00:02:14.430
Spurned by his daughter's encouragement, Luke
arrives at the church before the ceremony

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.819
and tells Tally the truth – the whole truth,
and nothing but.

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:21.970
He reveals everything about his past as a
CIA agent, explaining how it was the reason

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.870
for his odd behavior all those years ago and
how he kept it a secret to protect his family.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.040
Then, all of a sudden, Luke's car explodes
outside of the church.

00:02:29.585 --> 00:02:34.650
It goes from church bells to Hell's bells,
as terrorists swarm the ceremony and start firing.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:38.460
Luke and Emma pull out their weapons and return
the gunfire, revealing themselves as something

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.849
much more to the wedding guests.

00:02:39.849 --> 00:02:44.659
A burnt-looking Boro reappears, holding Tally
at gunpoint and demanding revenge.

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:48.350
In a typical dastardly villainous monologue,
he discusses how he survived the explosion

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.909
and found Emma and Luke.

00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:53.141
His nefarious plan is for them to shoot each
other in front of their loved ones.

00:02:53.141 --> 00:02:56.171
"The two of you – the two liars!

00:02:56.171 --> 00:03:01.800
– face each other, take your guns, and point
them at each other's heads."

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.740
Tally uses the medal that Luke showed her
as proof of his past to stab and unstabilize

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.599
Boro, who then takes a hail of bullets from
Emma and Luke.

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:12.170
However, both father and daughter understand
this is only the start of their problems since

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.530
their true identities have been compromised
and they believe Boro might have sold the

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:16.670
information to others.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.220
A black van arrives and Luke, Emma, Tally,
Donnie, Carter, Barry, Aldon, Roo, and the

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.510
rest of the family, including Oscar Brunner
and his family jump in.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.100
It's made clear that everyone's life is about
to change and they can no longer go back to

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.100
how it was before.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.680
Luke even describes the situation as being
particularly "FUBAR" – f—ed up beyond

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.680
all repair.

00:03:34.971 --> 00:03:38.739
"FUBAR" Season 1 is all about secrets and
the damage they cause in the long run.

00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:42.390
It's also abundantly obvious that the lack
of honesty is behind Luke and Tally's marriage

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.069
falling apart in the first place.

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:47.700
She believes he sells gym equipment for a
living and is a generally unreliable human

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.330
being who lets her down.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.500
Luke did have the chance to come clean to
her, though, when they reignited their relationship

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.500
in this season.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.434
His plan for retirement was already in place,
so he could have been honest much earlier.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.672
But he lied again

00:03:58.927 --> 00:04:00.522
"You deserve to know the truth…

00:04:04.182 --> 00:04:05.909
Barry has a gambling problem."

00:04:05.909 --> 00:04:09.220
He puts her through the wringer yet again
by luring her in, and dumping her when it

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.230
becomes serious.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:15.271
Then, once he realizes he may lose her forever
to Donnie, he unloads everything on her wedding day.

00:04:15.271 --> 00:04:18.324
While it might sound like a grand gesture
to win her back, it isn't.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.670
It shows a bit of Luke's selfishness and trust
issues.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:24.420
He might hide behind the fact that he's protecting
her and the family from potential danger by

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:28.070
not disclosing what he really does, but being
a part of their lives and in that line of

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:30.590
work will always put them at risk -- as the
finale proves.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:34.220
The least he could have afforded her was the
truth from the start.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.860
He only told her now because she was about
to get married to someone else, and he didn't

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:37.860
like it.

00:04:38.113 --> 00:04:43.039
The show features a lot of guns and fists
flying, but at its heart is, well, matters

00:04:43.039 --> 00:04:44.229
of the heart.

00:04:44.229 --> 00:04:48.199
The season finale leaves a question mark on
the status of two major love triangles -- and

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:51.730
no matter the outcome, some beloved characters
will be left brokenhearted here.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.970
The first involves Luke, Tally, and Donnie.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:57.270
Anyone can see that Luke and Tally share a
deep connection and it has never gone away

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.410
despite their divorce.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.850
Plus, they realize the sparks still exist
after their latest fling.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.860
Then, there's Donnie -- a nice guy who has
genuine feelings for Tally.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.590
He might not have the bluster of Luke, but
he treats Tally well and is there for her

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.590
when she needs him.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.245
"I mean, he's trying to replace me.

00:05:11.245 --> 00:05:13.757
He's cuckolding the entire family."

00:05:13.757 --> 00:05:15.479
"Please stop saying that."

00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:19.130
With all three together now, it remains to
be seen if Luke will make a play for Tally

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.050
in front of Donnie, or if Tally will admit
her feelings for Luke.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:26.199
In all likelihood, it looks like Donnie will
be the biggest loser in this situation.

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:29.320
Then, there's the drama between Emma, Aldon,
and Carter.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.569
Much like Donnie, Carter is the secure, reliable
option for Emma.

00:05:32.569 --> 00:05:36.380
However, Aldon possesses a more dangerous
and seductive appeal.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.919
She has already cheated on Carter with Aldon,
and it's evident there are also feelings there.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:43.940
While Carter and Emma may be broken up, there's
a hint they may try to work things out again.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.060
However, Aldon might have something to say
about that.

00:05:46.568 --> 00:05:50.919
After the gunfire in the church, no one has
much time to process what just happened.

00:05:50.919 --> 00:05:54.229
It's understandable; the adrenaline must be
through the roof and they are more concerned

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:56.620
about their safety than anything else at the
moment.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.669
However, once the dust settles, the noggins
will start ticking and questions will be asked.

00:06:00.669 --> 00:06:04.830
Imagine how someone like Oscar must feel knowing
his father and sister are CIA agents and he

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:05.830
never knew about it.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:09.640
Surely, he must feel a sense of betrayal at
how they kept this from him for so long.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.341
"So you're all CIA?"

00:06:12.341 --> 00:06:14.602
"No, just me.

00:06:14.821 --> 00:06:16.860
And Luke.

00:06:17.188 --> 00:06:18.188
And Emma."

00:06:18.188 --> 00:06:20.370
Similarly, spare a thought for poor Carter.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.820
He already believes the relationship between
him and Emma consisted of lies.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:28.110
Now, this extra bit of additional info will
make him question everything about their relationship,

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.860
including if it was even real in the first
place.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:34.480
Make no mistake about it, Luke and Emma have
a lot of explaining to do to their friends

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.480
and family here.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.805
They won't be able to brush this incident
under the carpet.

00:06:38.095 --> 00:06:41.599
Tina doesn't make it to the church as Barry's
date since she's wrapping something up at

00:06:41.599 --> 00:06:42.344
the office.

00:06:42.344 --> 00:06:45.479
She receives a call and suddenly, she switches
from English to Russian.

00:06:45.479 --> 00:06:47.280
"I'll call you later.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.970
I'm in the middle of something."

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.260
It's a shocking moment that leaves the audience
with a lot of questions about Tina and her

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.710
real motivations.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.979
At the start of "FUBAR" Season 1, Tina arrives
on the scene as a transfer from another department.

00:06:58.979 --> 00:07:02.990
She starts a romance with Barry and quickly
earns the trust of the rest of the team.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.990
Later, she reveals to Barry that she is meant
to be transferred out again.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:09.760
Undeterred, he pulls internal strings and
calls on a few favors to ensure she stays

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.360
where she is, so they can continue their relationship.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.390
However, the big reveal in the season finale
indicates that Tina may not be who she claims

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.390
to be.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.629
There's a possibility that she could be a
double agent and working with adversaries

00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:25.350
to infiltrate the CIA -- including faking
a relationship with Barry to gain his trust.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:29.610
Equally concerning is the identity of the
person on the opposite end of her phone call.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:33.150
Is it her real boss or potentially the villain
for another season of the show?

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:38.156
Despite Luke and Emma's fears, none of their
loved ones are actually hurt in "FUBAR" Season 1.

00:07:38.156 --> 00:07:42.994
They escape Boro's wrath relatively unscathed,
which means they are incredibly lucky and fortunate.

00:07:42.994 --> 00:07:46.740
However, neither of those elements makes for
riveting television shows, so this is merely

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.490
the calm before the storm.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:52.090
Saving all the main characters here, it's
a sure sign that there is major trouble brewing

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:54.000
down the road for the protagonists.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.300
In essence, Luke and Emma haven't suffered
at all.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.919
Boro wanted revenge against them for what
they did to him and for messing up his plans,

00:07:59.919 --> 00:08:01.740
but he didn't succeed in the slightest.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.900
The worst thing he did is reveal their secret
to their family and friends..

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:08.740
That being said, there is potential danger
on the horizon, especially considering the

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.480
group of untrained and unarmed people with
them now.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:15.349
While no one doubts Luke, Emma, and the rest
of the CIA's crew's ability to defend themselves,

00:08:15.349 --> 00:08:19.191
they are surrounded by regular folk, who make
the best targets for rogues.

00:08:19.191 --> 00:08:21.769
"Oh man, I picked the wrong day to get high."

00:08:21.769 --> 00:08:25.850
Unless "FUBAR" takes a drastic left turn,
it's likely the audience has seen the last

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:26.850
of Boro.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:30.440
There's no chance he survived all those bullets
to the chest, and Roo makes sure he's done

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.510
by popping him one more time for good measure.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.450
So, that's the curtain call on his time as
the villain of the show.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:39.433
As Luke states, though, it's uncertain how
many others know Luke and Emma's real identities now.

00:08:39.433 --> 00:08:43.340
Boro could have sold the information to the
highest bidder or even offered it up voluntarily

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:45.400
as a middle finger to the Brunners.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.890
Perhaps he might have told a few of the other
insidious characters he interacted with earlier

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.104
in the season.

00:08:50.104 --> 00:08:53.790
Alternatively, there's the real possibility
that Tina and the mysterious person she spoke

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.610
to on the phone could be revealed as the next
antagonists here.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:09:00.279
If she has been a double agent all along,
this could be the next phase of some master

00:09:00.279 --> 00:09:04.115
plan – one we may learn more about in a
potential FUBAR season 2.

